WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.501
-Welcome back to the show.
-Thank you.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.400
-It's...
-[ Chuckles ] Amazing.

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.534
It's wonderful to be here.
-It means so much

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:08.100
to have an actor
come on the show

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:09.467
that can talk
about their project.

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.400
-It's great --
-It's a big deal for us.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.801
You're our first --
-Thank you. Thank you, yeah.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you so much.

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:16.834
-It's really good to be here.
I'm really grateful to you.

00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:21.300
-I want to talk about "Loki,"
and congrats on that Season 2.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.534
But I also want to talk about --
you did this thing.

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:24.801
I think you do it annually.

00:00:24.801 --> 00:00:27.434
It's an England vs. the World
soccer match.

00:00:27.434 --> 00:00:28.767
-Soccer Aid. Yes.
-Yes.

00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:30.901
-It's called Soccer Aid
for UNICEF.

00:00:30.901 --> 00:00:34.667
And it's basically
this extraordinary event

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.300
at a big soccer stadium
in England.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.734
It was Old Trafford,

00:00:37.734 --> 00:00:40.200
where Manchester United play
this summer in June.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.367
And you -- basically former pros
and keen amateurs like myself.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.067
-Yeah, I mean,
you're really good.

00:00:47.067 --> 00:00:48.834
-No, no, no, no, no, no, no, no.
Come on, Jimmy.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:51.133
I am -- I'm a --
I said "keen amateur," like...

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:52.634
-I mean, no, but, no, no, no --
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:52.634 --> 00:00:53.734
No, I'm playing up
against people

00:00:53.734 --> 00:00:55.601
like Paul Scholes
and Francesco Totti...

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.434
-Not them, yeah.
-...you know, Roberto Carlos.

00:00:57.434 --> 00:00:58.467
Yeah. So...
-Yeah.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:00:59.701
Not counting them out.
-Yeah.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:00.834
-You're the best.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:01:00.834 --> 00:01:02.467
-I mean, yeah.
-Yeah, well, you know.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.133
-If you don't mention the other
players, you're number one.

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:05.501
-Exactly. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:05.501 --> 00:01:06.767
-Forget about Paul Scholes.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:09.033
Anyway, so --
so it was this summer,

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:11.033
and it's England versus
the rest of the world.

00:01:11.033 --> 00:01:12.901
And we raise loads of money
for children.

00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:15.400
-Good for you.
-Yeah. It was -- It was fun.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
And it was fun.

00:01:16.834 --> 00:01:20.000
I played --
I played for England,

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.334
not for the rest of the world.
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.868
And...
-Did you win?

00:01:23.868 --> 00:01:25.701
-We didn't, sadly.
-Yeah, okay. The world won.

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.200
-The world won.
-Okay. The world won.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.601
-But that's good for the world.
-We're rooting for the world.

00:01:28.601 --> 00:01:29.701
-We're rooting for the world,
always.

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.133
-Absolutely, yes.
-But it was hilarious.

00:01:31.133 --> 00:01:34.000
I mean, in training we had --
we -- there was a --

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.033
there was a moment where,
like -- 'cause I --

00:01:36.033 --> 00:01:38.868
as I say, I'm keen,
maybe not entirely skillful,

00:01:38.868 --> 00:01:41.100
but I put in a bit
of a sort of hard challenge

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:42.534
on my opposite number.

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.534
And she was like, "Oh, ref,
did you see that challenge?"

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:45.767
And the ref was like,
"He's Loki.

00:01:45.767 --> 00:01:47.067
He's using his magical powers.
What can I do?"

00:01:47.067 --> 00:01:48.400
-Yeah, exactly.
Yeah, you can use that.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.601
But I saw you running
with Usain Bolt.

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:53.634
-Well, so, this is a kickoff.
I didn't -- I was playing right,

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:55.634
on the right wing,
defensive midfielder.

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:58.200
And I look up to see
who I'm man-marking,

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:01.067
and it's the fastest man alive.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:02.567
-That's like -- That's the best.
-It's like, "Okay, good luck."

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:03.934
-That's the best challenge
in the world.

00:02:03.934 --> 00:02:05.033
-"Good luck." Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-You're like -- Yeah.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:06.400
-Absolutely amazing.
-Yeah.

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:08.868
-I mean -- he's -- when you --
when you hear --

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:10.968
you see
the legs coming towards you,

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.067
it's like an express train.

00:02:12.067 --> 00:02:13.067
-No. Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:15.434
-He's the fastest.
Yeah. Here's you.

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.367
I think you're kind of
holding your own there.

00:02:17.367 --> 00:02:18.567
-He's floating, you notice.

00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:19.734
He's --
-Yeah.

00:02:19.734 --> 00:02:21.133
-He's, like,
still walking on water.

00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:22.901
-Yeah.
-Let me see.

00:02:22.901 --> 00:02:25.067
There's one of you --
Here's what I wanted to show.

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:27.567
You should frame this.
-[ Chuckling ] Okay.

00:02:27.567 --> 00:02:29.133
-This is you running alongside
Usain Bolt.

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:30.367
Look at this.
-Look at this guy.

00:02:30.367 --> 00:02:31.601
-Not bad.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:31.601 --> 00:02:34.434
-[ Laughs ]
-Not bad. Respect!

00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:37.734
-Yeah. I mean...
-The form. The form. The form.

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:41.267
-Yeah, I like to think --
I don't know if it's the angle,

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.434
but in this photograph,
I'm ahead of him.

00:02:43.434 --> 00:02:45.434
-Yeah, that's exactly right.
Thank you. That's --

00:02:45.434 --> 00:02:46.667
That's all that matters.
Frame this.

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:47.934
-But the determination,
honestly --

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.400
and I said to him afterwards --
-He's the best.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.234
-He's the best. Like,
he's a real football fan --

00:02:51.234 --> 00:02:52.601
soccer fan -- sorry --
I should say.

00:02:52.601 --> 00:02:56.534
-No, of course.
-And I love running.

00:02:56.534 --> 00:02:59.033
And it's a big part of my life.
And he's just an icon for me.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:01.133
I mean, he's like
an international sports icon.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:03.000
-Yeah.
-And to go against him

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.667
was just like such a thrill
and privilege.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.501
-No, but he's running next to
you, going like, "That's Loki!"

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:08.934
[ Laughter ]
-He had a few laughs.

00:03:08.934 --> 00:03:10.734
You know, he -- I think
I gave him a few problems,

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:13.501
'cause, obviously,
he's unbelievably quick.

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:15.033
-Yeah.
-And so people just want

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.100
to swing the ball over to him,

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:17.400
and he'll put it
in the back of the net.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:19.200
But -- But I was --
I was -- I stuck to him.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.367
You know, I held my own.
-You did a great job.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.200
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:25.067
I want to talk about --

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:26.934
Let's talk about "Loki"
while we -- we can do it now.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:28.667
-We're here. We're here, yeah.
-We're allowed to talk about it.

00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.701
-We're allowed to talk about it.
-Season 2 was great!

00:03:30.701 --> 00:03:32.601
-Thank you. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:32.601 --> 00:03:35.400
-It was great!
-Thank you so much.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.868
-And we couldn't discuss
Season 2,

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:38.167
but now we can discuss it.

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:40.067
The season finale is --

00:03:40.067 --> 00:03:42.067
you can get the whole Season 2
on Disney+ right now.

00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:43.000
I don't want to spoil it.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.267
No spoilers.
-Yeah.

00:03:44.267 --> 00:03:45.601
-If you're watching,
we will not spoil it.

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.501
But what can we say --

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.400
what can we say
about the finale?

00:03:49.400 --> 00:03:52.100
-I mean, if you haven't seen it,
no, I will not spoil it for you.

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:56.767
But I will say this -- it --
it all comes full circle.

00:03:56.767 --> 00:03:58.901
[ Audience oohs ]
And...

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:01.367
-Yeah. That's a great --
Well, you know how to --

00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:03.467
He knows how to do it. Yeah.
He knows how to do it.

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:05.133
-Yeah. I mean,
it is a kind of -- it's --

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:06.734
it's the conclusion to Season 2.

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:09.100
It's also a conclusion
to seasons 1 and 2.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.033
It's also the conclusion to --

00:04:11.033 --> 00:04:16.334
to 6 films and 12 episodes
and 14 years of my life.

00:04:16.334 --> 00:04:18.501
It's -- And so -- And in --
I think, in the finale --

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:19.734
-Has it been 14 years?
-14 years.

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.501
I was 29 when I was cast.

00:04:21.501 --> 00:04:22.734
I'm 42 now.

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:24.400
-Wow, bud.
-It's been a journey.

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:25.734
-Good for you.
Congratulations.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.234
-Thank you. But -- But --
-You did a great job.

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:28.701
-Thank you.
-You've done a great job.

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.567
-But in the -- in the finale,

00:04:30.567 --> 00:04:36.000
I do think, in the finale,
there are echoes and resonances

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:39.467
of every version of Loki
that I've played.

00:04:39.467 --> 00:04:40.901
And I think,
without spoiling it,

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:44.801
I think it all -- the episode is
called "Glorious Purpose."

00:04:44.801 --> 00:04:46.601
-Oh, that's your line.
-And if you remember,

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:49.334
in the first "Avengers" film,
Loki comes down to Earth,

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:51.601
looks straight at Sam Jackson
as Nick Fury,

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:53.100
and I say, "I'm Loki of Asgard.

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.033
I'm burdened with
glorious purpose."

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.734
And he's arrogant,
and he's hubristic,

00:04:56.734 --> 00:04:58.868
and he's entitled,
and he's puffed up,

00:04:58.868 --> 00:05:00.868
and he's going to take
over the world.

00:05:00.868 --> 00:05:03.901
And then, you know,
it doesn't go so well for him.

00:05:03.901 --> 00:05:05.434
We've all seen "Infinity War."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:05.434 --> 00:05:07.801
Face-to-face with Thanos.
-Yes.

00:05:07.801 --> 00:05:09.701
-Not so glorious.
-Yeah.

00:05:09.701 --> 00:05:11.300
-At the beginning of Season 1,

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:13.133
Mobius, played by Owen Wilson --
the best ever.

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:15.200
-He's so good in this.
-So great.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.634
-He's great, and he's also
really funny in this, too.

00:05:16.634 --> 00:05:17.868
-He's hilarious.
-Yeah.

00:05:17.868 --> 00:05:19.000
-But he basically shows Loki

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:21.767
that the glorious purpose
was a fallacy.

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:25.067
And he gets kind of
a second chance.

00:05:25.067 --> 00:05:28.968
And that, I think, was the most
exciting thing about this show

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:32.334
was seeing Loki try to rethink
and rediscover

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:35.100
that sense of purpose,
which we can all relate to.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.534
I think, you know, we all wonder

00:05:38.534 --> 00:05:41.467
if we're in charge
of our own story.

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:42.701
-Yeah.
-You know, can we --

00:05:42.701 --> 00:05:45.000
can a leopard change his spots?

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:47.534
Do we have any free will?

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:49.334
And in exercising
your free will,

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:51.067
you make choices
in your own life.

00:05:51.067 --> 00:05:52.367
You get a -- I don't know --

00:05:52.367 --> 00:05:54.501
you get a black coffee
or a latte or a cappuccino.

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:55.968
That's a choice.
I mean, it's a small choice.

00:05:55.968 --> 00:05:58.400
-It's all choices.
-But, yeah, every -- every --

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.033
every choice you make adds up
to the picture of your life.

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:05.067
And do those choices
inform your purpose?

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:07.501
And I think all of us as people
want happy lives,

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:09.667
but we also want lives
with a purpose.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.067
And that's really what the show
is talking about.

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:13.734
-Yeah. I-I-I -- It's very good.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.734 --> 00:06:16.400
That's a way -- a great way to
describe it without spoiling it.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.400
-In the end,
it comes back to, like,

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.067
meaning and identity
and family,

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:22.801
which is really what "Loki"
has always been about.

00:06:22.801 --> 00:06:25.033
It's always been about
purpose and family.

00:06:25.033 --> 00:06:27.067
-There's a lot of fans
that have some --

00:06:27.067 --> 00:06:31.100
some theories about the show
and the finale.

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:32.200
-Okay.
-And I was thinking maybe

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.667
I could run through
a few theories.

00:06:33.667 --> 00:06:36.000
Again, none of these are true,
maybe -- or maybe they aren't.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.300
You're going to...
-Okay.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.300
-...answer the best you can.
-I love a fan theory.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:39.467
-Yeah, you don't mind?

00:06:39.467 --> 00:06:40.467
-I don't know how much
I'll be able to say,

00:06:40.467 --> 00:06:41.934
but [chuckles]
I'll give it a go.

00:06:41.934 --> 00:06:44.200
-Okay, one theory --
is there a secret connection

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:47.834
